By Lemma \ref{b1b2} and Theorem \ref{t8}, $d (\mathbf{y} ,w)$ is of type $\binom{ \ast  ,k}{ \ast  ,g}$$\binom{ \ast }{ \ast  ,k ,g}$$\binom{ \ast  ,k ,g}{ \ast }$ for $g \in B_{1}$ and $k \in B_{2}$, i.e. each column of $d (\mathbf{y} ,w)$ is of type $\binom{ \ast  ,k}{ \ast  ,g}$ or $\binom{ \ast }{ \ast  ,k ,g}$ or $\binom{ \ast  ,k ,g}{ \ast }$ and there are columns of types $\binom{ \ast  ,k}{ \ast  ,g}$ and $\binom{ \ast }{ \ast  ,k ,g}$ and $\binom{ \ast  ,k ,g}{ \ast }$ in $d (\mathbf{y} ,w)$. This immediately gives the following corollary. 


