Rejected honestly on hardness.

The paper’s Theorem 1 and Section 13 provide a polynomial LP/network-flow method, ruling out Track A. The attempted Track B construction passed local G1–G9 checks, but every oracle solved it: 9/9 overall and 3/3 at the hardest preset. The compact 292-operation route was therefore too accessible. See the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.06393).

