The construction is viable as Track B. I’m using the paper’s own Section 3 object—a saturated job–machine matrix decomposed into “columns” (perfect matchings)—and planting a compact affine decomposition over a prime field. The paper’s polynomial machinery remains fully acknowledged; the benchmark gap is between thousands of exact matching/line checks and a sub-300-operation invariant route, not a complexity-theoretic claim.
